  p(f'We evaluate the explicit coefficient $C_0=1025$ for Wang\textquotesingle s support-size tester, conditional on the accompanying proof and with $L_0=1024$ unchanged. The frozen main design comprises {s["primary_independent_poisson_paths"]:,} independent simulated Poisson-process paths and {s["primary_method_trial_evaluations"]:,} paired method evaluations. Synthetic sizes range from $1$ to $10^{{12}}$ across five separation parameters and up to fifteen distribution scenarios. Ten published empirical populations cover trees, mites, birds, spiders, moths, snails, and fish. No errors are observed for $C_0=1025$ in the promised primary cells; worst simultaneous 95\% error upper bounds are {100*syn.worst_simultaneous_upper:.3f}\% on synthetic and {100*nat.worst_simultaneous_upper:.3f}\% on empirical populations. However, all practical sizes use the observed-count branch, a simple certified count baseline requires fewer samples, and only {s["natural_budget_sufficient_cells"]} of {s["natural_budget_cells"]} ecological configurations have as many original records as the prescribed mean. Correlation stress tests expose violations of the iid requirement. Full-degree interval checks and public-API executions support implementation fidelity without substituting for a universal proof or a field validation.')
