  p(f'Only {s["natural_budget_sufficient_cells"]}/{s["natural_budget_cells"]} ecological configurations have $N\ge m_{{1025}}$. We also report $\Pr\{{\operatorname{{Poi}}(m)>N\}}$, because $N\ge m$ alone does not guarantee a feasible Poisson draw. The only mean-feasible configurations are from the mite dataset. We run 200 finite-file Poisson subsampling attempts for each and retain every overflow rather than redrawing. These without-replacement file analyses are descriptive: the underlying spatial core collection has not been established to be an iid sample from the desired external population. For insufficient files, resampling with replacement does not create additional independent ecological evidence.')
