  p(f'We test two controlled departures from independence while retaining the same marginal species distribution: identical-label duplication and multiple labels drawn within real abundance-weighted groups. Their worst observed false-negative rates are {100*s["duplication_worst_error"]:.3f}\% and {100*s["group_stress_worst_error"]:.3f}\%, respectively. These deliberate stresses are not estimates of natural field dependence. Selecting a group independently for every individual with probability proportional to its abundance recovers the pooled empirical iid target; batching individuals within the same selected group does not.')
